Hello everyone,
It's been a while I have been trying to enable the gzip compression on my nginx for my shiny server. But no success so far, no matter how much I have read the tutorials or how many different thing I have tried. Is there anybody know how to enable that ?
Thanks

This is how my configuration looks like:
/etc/nginx/nginx.conf

http {

##
# Basic Settings
##
client_max_body_size 1000M;
sendfile on;
tcp_nopush on;
tcp_nodelay on;
client_body_timeout 30;
client_header_timeout 30;
send_timeout 10;
keepalive_disable none;
types_hash_max_size 2048;

gzip on;
gzip_disable "msie6";

gzip_vary on;
gzip_proxied any;
gzip_comp_level 6;
gzip_buffers 16 8k;
gzip_http_version 1.1;
gzip_min_length 256;
gzip_types text/plain text/css application/json application/x-javascript text/xml application/xml application/xml+rss text/javascript application/vnd.ms-fontobject application/x-font-ttf font/opentype image/svg+xml image/x-icon;
include /etc/nginx/conf.d/*.conf;
include /etc/nginx/sites-enabled/*;
}

/etc/nginx/sites-enabled/defualt

server {
listen   80; ## listen for ipv4; this line is default and implied
#listen   [::]:80 default ipv6only=on; ## listen for ipv6

root /usr/share/nginx/www;
index index.php index.html index.htm;

# Make site accessible from http://localhost/
server_name localhost;

location /shiny/ {
 rewrite ^(/shiny/[^/]+)$ $1/ permanent;
 proxy_pass http://127.0.0.1:3838/shiny/;
   proxy_http_version 1.1;
            proxy_read_timeout 20d;
             keepalive_disable none;
             proxy_set_header Upgrade $http_upgrade;
             proxy_set_header Connection "upgrade";

}
}

You are proxying the request, so that will not be gzipped.

After that, shiny server is handling the request, so no gzip will happen.

Erik

