Hi,
I have a rather complex shiny app with tabs containing numerous of observers and renderers, and imbricated renderers.
I would like to be able to save and restore data in a certain order, as some values depend on other values. The priority argument would have been perfect for what I'm trying to do, but there is no such argument for the renderUI function. I know that I can use uiOutput and outputOptions to control priority, but my imbricated renderUI are not in the output object.

output$try <- renderUI({
  if (input$test == 1) renderUI(...)
  else renderUI(...)
})

Therefore, I was thinking about using onFlush(ed) function to record the last flushing time, wait 2 seconds and then restore another tab. Unfortunately, that does not work as it creates an infinite loop. Example:

ui = function(request) {
  fluidPage(
      title = "test",
      id = "main",
      uiOutput("testUI"),
  )
}

server <- shinyServer(function(session, input, output) {
  values <- reactiveValues(last_flush = Sys.time())

  onFlushed(function(){
    values$last_flush <- Sys.time()
  }, once = FALSE)

  output$testUI <- renderUI({
    actionButton("clickButton", "Click here")
  })

  observe({
    print(values$last_flush)
  })

})

shinyApp(ui, server)

Do you have any suggestion on how I could perform what I'm trying to do?
Cheers!

